  - level: 10
    grants: ["Roll on the Neurosis Table"]
  - level: 12
    grants: ["Roll on the Psychosis Table", "+2 O.C.C. Related Skills", "+1 Secondary Skill"]
  - level: 14
    grants: ["Roll for a Random Insanity"]
restrictions:
  - "Race Limitation: The M.O.M. process is designed for humans, but will also work on Ogres. D-Bees and other races attempting M.O.M. implants have a 01-80% likelihood of the character being accidentally lobotomized (roll up a new character); rare nonhuman successes do NOT induce psionic abilities and instead cause one extra insanity immediately and another at levels 4, 8 and 10, all rolled on the Random Insanity Table in the Rules Section."
  - "M.O.M. implants do not work on supernatural beings or creatures of magic."
  - "Cybernetics: absolutely none, other than the M.O.M. implants."
  - "Additional weapons, gear and vehicles may be issued on assignment, and the Lightning Warrior may acquire and keep weapons, armor and items from the outside world, demon slaying and magic items included, for missions away from the Geofront."
side_effects: "The M.O.M. conversion has a tendency to wear out the human body and has a number of unpleasant and unavoidable side effects, the worst of which is mental illness; over time, every recipient of M.O.M. suffers from increasing mental instability (hence ''Crazies''). This manifests as an escalating series of insanity rolls at set experience levels (see level_progression) that can lead to multiple personalities and delusions."
extraction_notes: "DECLARED COPY: printed 133-134 says to roll the Lightning Warrior up as any Crazy (Rifts RPG), with O.C.C. Skills the same as CS Special Forces with additions and substitutions, and related skills, secondary skills and equipment the same as the Crazy. This is a full copy of production''s crazy (pools, bonuses, psionics, abilities, insanity, related and secondary skills, equipment) and of cs-special-forces (O.C.C. skills and MOS), with the printed changes applied. No copy_of is declared: the book changes most blocks. GROUP: the book''s Elite Geofront Forces section (printed 128), so men-of-arms. ATTRIBUTE REQUIREMENTS: I.Q. 9 and a willingness to undergo the process (the Crazy prints none). S.D.C.: 6D6+50 is stored as sdc_base, and the Crazy''s Super Endurance +3D6x10 S.D.C. and +5D6 hit points are kept as pool bonuses; the book says nothing on whether 6D6+50 includes the augmentation, so a reader who takes it as the whole figure would drop the Crazy''s pools. BONUSES: in addition to the Crazy''s, +1 initiative, +2 disarm, +2 pull punch and +2 save vs possession, summed into the stored figures (initiative 3, possession 4). The Demon Slaying Frenzy bonuses are conditional and are a special ability. I.S.P.: M.E. x2 +1D10 per level replaces the Crazy''s 6D6+M.E. formula; the Crazy''s three minor psionic powers are KEPT, since the book says Lightning Warriors have all the usual M.O.M. abilities, and Mystic Martial Art Power is None. SKILLS: the Special Forces list with Language: Chinese at 98% replacing the native American; Literacy: Chinese (+15%), Pilot: Bicycle (+10%) and Disguise (+15%) added; Prowl at +20% in place of +15%; Mathematics: Basic (+20%) equals the base''s; Pilot: Robots & Power Armor substituted by Pilot Hover Vehicle (+10%), stored as Hover Craft (ground); Robot Combat Elite thrown out. The Crazy''s own O.C.C. skill list is not used. HAND TO HAND: Western Martial Arts substituted by a pick of Dog Boxing, Monkey Style or Drunken Style; the book sells no other style, so costs is empty, and the Crazy''s Assassin and Commando options are gone. EQUIPMENT: the Crazy''s list with the printed substitutions - Lightning Warrior Armor (stored as the Shadow Armor row, with the plated M.D.C. in the note; the catalog has no row for the plated suit), a Vibro-Knife or Vibro-Sword, one each of the GHT-88, GHT-89, GHT-95 and GHT-93 pistols with six clips each, one conventional M.D. rifle (the GHF-AK47, the only Geofront rifle in the catalog) and one Chi Rifle or heavy weapon, in place of the Crazy''s armor, hatchet, knives, ancient weapons, energy handgun, energy rifle and E-clips. MONEY: 2D6x100 credits; monthly salary 900 credits, with basic needs provided by the government. CYBERNETICS: absolutely none (the Crazy allowed optics, lungs and weapon implants). ALIGNMENT: any; typically 10% Principled, 30% Scrupulous, 20% Unprincipled, 30% Anarchist, 10% Aberrant or other. XP: the Blind Mystic, Chi Commando and Lightning Warriors ladder, printed 160, read off a render."
---

## Lore

Lightning Warriors are the Geofront''s Crazies. They carry the same M.O.M.
implants and the same creeping instability as the Crazies of the West, but
martial arts training before and after the process gives them far more
self-control. Between fights they meditate or run through practice forms; to
ordinary people they seem cool, distant, restless or simply bored, waiting for
the next chance to act.

They hate the Yama Kings and hunt demons with something close to obsession,
yet stay loyal to the Geofront and avoid hopeless battles. In combat they are
never still, and what looks like reckless abandon is a series of measured
risks judged in an instant.

## GM Notes

Outside China every Chi-based power weakens (printed 141): the Chi pool, the
Chi a character can draw on, and the range, duration and damage of Chi powers
are halved, combat bonuses from Mystic Martial Art Powers drop by one, and
characters above sixth level lose one attack per melee. None of this is
stored.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'geofront-lightning-warrior');


